# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Applications are private.
#
# An application file describes one joint on one real robot: payload, geometry,
# the bus voltage your robot supplies, the ambient inside your shell. That is
# proprietary design data, and the reports and charts generated beside it are
# too. This repo is public, so the whole directory is ignored by default.
#
# The bundled examples are deliberately exempted so a fresh clone can still run
# the quick start in the README. Keep real work out of applications/examples/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/applications/*
!/applications/examples/
!/applications/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw vendor datasheets are kept locally, not committed.
#
# The JSON in db/actuators/ is the reviewable artifact: it carries the numbers
# we actually use, each with a source, a tolerance, and a note naming the
# datasheet section it came from. The PDFs behind it are large (several MB
# each, vs. a few KB per JSON file), do not diff, and are vendor copyright, so
# redistributing them from a public Apache-2.0 repo is not ours to do.
#
# Drop them in db/datasheets/ named to match the actuator file they support
# (robstride_00.pdf <-> robstride_00.json) so the provenance notes stay
# checkable by anyone who has fetched their own copy from the vendor.
#
# The README documenting that convention is exempted so it survives a clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/actuator_eval/db/datasheets/*
!/actuator_eval/db/datasheets/README.md

# Generated results, wherever they land.
*_report_*.txt
*_charts_*.html

# ...but the committed reference example outputs stay tracked. These names must
# match what eval_actuator.py actually writes (<application>_<actuator>), or the
# exemptions silently stop applying -- they did, after an earlier rename.
!/applications/examples/elbow_example_robstride_00_report.txt
!/applications/examples/elbow_example_robstride_00.html
!/applications/examples/elbow_envelope_example_robstride_00_report.txt
!/applications/examples/elbow_envelope_example_robstride_00.html

# Captured envelopes are the user's own operating data, like applications, so
# they stay out of the repo -- but the bundled example is public so a fresh
# clone can run the envelope path without a robot.
/envelopes/*
!/envelopes/examples/
!/envelopes/examples/*.json

# Claude Code project instructions are local-only.
CLAUDE.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

